      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I hear how incredibly painful and isolating this grief feels, especially when it makes you question your own identity. It is completely understandable to feel like a ghost when someone you loved so deeply leaves, taking a fundamental part of yourself with them. While this transition of \"unbecoming\" often feels permanent in the moment, many people find that over time, the defining traits of their partner are honored within the survivor rather than disappearing forever. Give yourself permission to feel this vast emptiness, knowing that healing is a process of rediscovering your identity piece by piece.",
